1
00:00:00,220 --> 00:00:03,139
Welcome to the fourth episode of earthlings
101.

2
00:00:03,139 --> 00:00:42,240
Today we will learn what good and evil is.

3
00:00:42,240 --> 00:00:46,190
The concept of good and evil is fundamental
to understanding human behaviour.

4
00:00:46,190 --> 00:00:51,550
As I explained in the first episode, the earthling
mind is divided into three parts: the ego,

5
00:00:51,550 --> 00:00:52,840
the beast and the niggler.

6
00:00:52,840 --> 00:00:57,270
The beast tells the ego what he wants to do,
and the niggler tells him what he should do.

7
00:00:57,270 --> 00:01:01,640
The Niggler is constantly commenting about
the ego's actions, approving some and rejecting

8
00:01:01,640 --> 00:01:02,640
others.

9
00:01:02,640 --> 00:01:06,440
This process is called self- awareness, and
the criteria the Niggler applies - that is

10
00:01:06,440 --> 00:01:08,659
actually good and evil.

11
00:01:08,659 --> 00:01:12,600
To enforce his judgement, the niggler punishes
"evil" actions with feelings like shame and

12
00:01:12,600 --> 00:01:17,810
guilt, and awards "good" actions with satisfaction
- just as the beast uses pleasure, pain, fear

13
00:01:17,810 --> 00:01:19,340
and desire to get what he wants.

14
00:01:19,340 --> 00:01:24,830
There is a myth, an ancient fictional story,
about what happened when earthlings became

15
00:01:24,830 --> 00:01:25,830
self-aware.

16
00:01:25,830 --> 00:01:31,280
The first two earthlings, so the story, lived
in a garden, a closed area with rich vegetation,

17
00:01:31,280 --> 00:01:33,720
guarded by some kind of bio-administrator.

18
00:01:33,720 --> 00:01:37,300
We will talk about this kind of creature in
a forthcoming episode.

19
00:01:37,300 --> 00:01:41,930
According to the story, the earthlings first
act as self-aware beings was to eat a fruit

20
00:01:41,930 --> 00:01:44,299
against the will of the bio-administrator.

21
00:01:44,299 --> 00:01:48,140
Doing so made them realize that some acts
are qualified as good, and some others as

22
00:01:48,140 --> 00:01:51,960
evil, in particular what they just had done:
eating a forbidden fruit.

23
00:01:51,960 --> 00:01:56,619
They were filled with guilt and shame, and
thrown out of the garden into a harsh wilderness.

24
00:01:56,619 --> 00:02:01,220
This story tells us aliens a lot about how
earthlings experience their own self-awareness.

25
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:06,549
It seems that self-awareness is extremely
uncomfortable, like living in a hostile environment.

26
00:02:06,549 --> 00:02:09,890
Having a niggler in one's brain must be like
having a brainsucker attached to one's head

27
00:02:09,890 --> 00:02:13,740
who is constantly babbling about what is or
isn't conform to the rules of the galactic

28
00:02:13,740 --> 00:02:15,020
bureaucracy.

29
00:02:15,020 --> 00:02:18,670
And guilt is probably as painful as the brain
acid released by a brainsucker when the host

30
00:02:18,670 --> 00:02:21,780
breaks one of the zillions of rules of the
bureaucracy.

31
00:02:21,780 --> 00:02:25,490
Except that the niggler doesn't care about
the bureaucracy - it has its own rules which

32
00:02:25,490 --> 00:02:29,030
have evolved through evolution and society
: good and evil.

33
00:02:29,030 --> 00:02:33,270
But what is this good and evil thing anyway,
and what is its purpose?

34
00:02:33,270 --> 00:02:36,720
Good and evil exist to encourage cooperation
between individuals.

35
00:02:36,720 --> 00:02:40,850
Basically, an action is "good" when it helps
the group, and "evil" when it goes against

36
00:02:40,850 --> 00:02:42,620
the interests of the group.

37
00:02:42,620 --> 00:02:46,050
Without cooperation enforced by the nigglers
in their brain, every earthling would only

38
00:02:46,050 --> 00:02:47,900
serve its own benefit.

39
00:02:47,900 --> 00:02:52,680
But, you might ask : if every member of the
group maximizes his own benefit, wouldn't

40
00:02:52,680 --> 00:02:56,020
this sum up and maximize the benefit of the
group?

41
00:02:56,020 --> 00:02:57,020
Actually not.

42
00:02:57,020 --> 00:03:00,890
There are situations where egoistically maximizing
one’s own benefit reduces the benefit of

43
00:03:00,890 --> 00:03:03,410
everybody, including of those being egoists.

44
00:03:03,410 --> 00:03:07,700
A textbook example is what earthlings call
"prisoners dilemma".

45
00:03:07,700 --> 00:03:12,820
Imagine that two galactic evildoers, Mighty
Cthulhu and Lord Xenu, are arrested and thrown

46
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:18,630
into prison by the galactic police for unauthorized
messing with planet earth - say, some clever

47
00:03:18,630 --> 00:03:21,410
scheme involving volcanoes and bad dreams.

48
00:03:21,410 --> 00:03:25,989
Unfortunately there are no witnesses for their
machinations, besides some disembodied thetans

49
00:03:25,989 --> 00:03:28,930
and mad cultists who don't legally count as
witnesses.

50
00:03:28,930 --> 00:03:33,560
So, the authorities interrogate both villains
separately, offering them reduction of prison

51
00:03:33,560 --> 00:03:35,129
time if they confess.

52
00:03:35,129 --> 00:03:39,490
Here is the deal: If none of them confesses,
the authority can't prove anything and both

53
00:03:39,490 --> 00:03:43,160
get only 100 years for unauthorized entering
a protected area.

54
00:03:43,160 --> 00:03:46,410
One triangle in the diagram corresponds to
100 years.

55
00:03:46,410 --> 00:03:50,270
If one of them confesses, he gets free, whereas
the other one gets the maximum penalty of

56
00:03:50,270 --> 00:03:51,920
800 years in prison.

57
00:03:51,920 --> 00:03:57,420
If both confess, both get a reduced penalty
of 400 years.

58
00:03:57,420 --> 00:04:01,880
From Lord Xenus point of view, the decision
seems clear: Whatever Cthulhu does, Xenu is

59
00:04:01,880 --> 00:04:03,450
better off confessing.

60
00:04:03,450 --> 00:04:07,970
If Cthulhu keeps his tentaculous mouth shut,
Xenu can avoid prison by betraying him.

61
00:04:07,970 --> 00:04:12,050
If Cthulhu betrays him, Xenu can reduce his
prison time by talking as well.

62
00:04:12,050 --> 00:04:16,260
The same holds for Cthulhu: No matter what
Xenu does, Cthulhu is better of betraying

63
00:04:16,260 --> 00:04:17,260
him.

64
00:04:17,260 --> 00:04:20,280
So, egoism might drive both villains to betraying
each other.

65
00:04:20,280 --> 00:04:24,570
But the point is, when both act egoistically
and talk, each one gets more prison time than

66
00:04:24,570 --> 00:04:26,419
when both cooperate and keep quiet.

67
00:04:26,419 --> 00:04:31,600
So, when both maximize their individual outcome,
this actually reduces the outcome for everybody.

68
00:04:31,600 --> 00:04:35,210
But even if both realize this and cooperate,
each one will still be tempted to betray the

69
00:04:35,210 --> 00:04:37,240
other one.

70
00:04:37,240 --> 00:04:40,630
Another example for this kind of situation
would be a clan of earthlings where everyone

71
00:04:40,630 --> 00:04:43,880
has one goat, a domestic animal which provides
milk.

72
00:04:43,880 --> 00:04:47,310
It won't take long for earthlings to figure
out that one can get a second goat by stealing

73
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:48,610
one during the night.

74
00:04:48,610 --> 00:04:52,250
So, goat thieves are better off than earthlings
who sleep during the night.

75
00:04:52,250 --> 00:04:56,491
However, if everybody becomes a goat thief,
everybody will end up with one goat, and the

76
00:04:56,491 --> 00:05:00,150
sneaky nocturnal goat exchange will be a complete
waste of time and energy.

77
00:05:00,150 --> 00:05:03,370
So the clan will have a disadvantage against
another clan who found a way to avoid stealing

78
00:05:03,370 --> 00:05:07,060
from each other every night and is well-rested
in the morning.

79
00:05:07,060 --> 00:05:10,340
This kind of situation is the basic problem
of human group behaviour.

80
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:13,620
The solution evolution found was the development
of the niggler and the concept of good and

81
00:05:13,620 --> 00:05:14,620
evil.

82
00:05:14,620 --> 00:05:18,191
If actions like stealing are evil, the niggler
will punish theft with remorse, a feeling

83
00:05:18,191 --> 00:05:21,660
which causes more discomfort than the milk
of the stolen goat causes pleasure.

84
00:05:21,660 --> 00:05:25,660
So, suddenly, stealing is far less appealing
than it was before.

85
00:05:25,660 --> 00:05:29,750
Likewise, if another member of the group happens
to have no goat, the niggler will push the

86
00:05:29,750 --> 00:05:31,940
individual to give some milk to the other
one.

87
00:05:31,940 --> 00:05:35,460
This holds even more if the poor individual
is a woman, as women are the bottleneck for

88
00:05:35,460 --> 00:05:36,919
population growth.

89
00:05:36,919 --> 00:05:40,750
Such selfless actions which help the group
are considered good, and are rewarded by the

90
00:05:40,750 --> 00:05:42,550
niggler with positive feelings.

91
00:05:42,550 --> 00:05:46,979
Of course, earthlings had to define what actions
are actually good and evil in the first place.

92
00:05:46,979 --> 00:05:51,050
So they developed sets of rules which are
transmitted from generation to generation.

93
00:05:51,050 --> 00:05:52,670
These rules are called ethics.

94
00:05:52,670 --> 00:05:54,490
Tips for tourists.

95
00:05:54,490 --> 00:05:58,750
Before visiting earth, familiarize yourself
with the basic rules of good and evil.

96
00:05:58,750 --> 00:06:03,229
Even a harmless act like abducting a cow is
considered evil and can get you into trouble.

97
00:06:03,229 --> 00:06:08,419
You don't want to spend the rest of your life
locked away in a secret government facility.

98
00:06:08,419 --> 00:06:11,400
As mentioned before, self awareness is extremely
unpleasant.

99
00:06:11,400 --> 00:06:15,290
So, earthlings try to silence their self-awareness
at any price.

100
00:06:15,290 --> 00:06:19,130
They stick to a daily routine without any
ethical decisions, they intoxicate their brain

101
00:06:19,130 --> 00:06:23,280
with drugs, they fill it with useless information,
they escape into fictional worlds, and they

102
00:06:23,280 --> 00:06:27,009
welcome every authority who tells them what
good and evil is - even if the actions suggested

103
00:06:27,009 --> 00:06:29,850
by the authority are obviously harmful for
the group.

104
00:06:29,850 --> 00:06:33,240
This leads to absurd and paradoxical situations
like millions following a religious leader

105
00:06:33,240 --> 00:06:36,900
who forbids a contraceptive device which could
actually slow down a dangerous pandemic and

106
00:06:36,900 --> 00:06:39,070
reduce overpopulation and famine.

107
00:06:39,070 --> 00:06:40,870
Scientific advice.

108
00:06:40,870 --> 00:06:45,030
An interesting field of research is experimental
ethics: Abduct an earthling and put him into

109
00:06:45,030 --> 00:06:46,400
a moral dilemma.

110
00:06:46,400 --> 00:06:50,400
For example whether to give rather food to
a starving man, or to a sexy woman.

111
00:06:50,400 --> 00:06:55,620
You might be surprised by the results.

112
00:06:55,620 --> 00:07:00,740
Actions considered evil typically include
killing, seizing land, raping, stealing, and

113
00:07:00,740 --> 00:07:03,870
lying, as these are actions which are harmful
for the group.

114
00:07:03,870 --> 00:07:07,240
Of course, this only holds when the actions
target members of the group.

115
00:07:07,240 --> 00:07:11,180
If applied to members of a hostile group,
earthlings apply other standards, and even

116
00:07:11,180 --> 00:07:15,560
use other words : In this case, killing is
called war, raping and stealing are called

117
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:20,480
spoils of war, seizing land is called conquest,
and lying is called diplomacy.

118
00:07:20,480 --> 00:07:24,440
Those actions are not only allowed but considered
good and honorful, as they help the group.

119
00:07:24,440 --> 00:07:27,600
Of course, the other group considers these
actions as evil.

120
00:07:27,600 --> 00:07:30,900
This leads to the double standards earthlings
apply in case of hostile groups.

121
00:07:30,900 --> 00:07:35,250
Consider two tribes, red and green, which
are in conflict with each other.

122
00:07:35,250 --> 00:07:39,490
Assume that the green tribesmen destroy some
buildings of the red tribe, killing people.

123
00:07:39,490 --> 00:07:42,169
This harms the red tribe and helps the green
one.

124
00:07:42,169 --> 00:07:45,789
In consequence, the action is evil for the
red guys but good for the green guys - not

125
00:07:45,789 --> 00:07:49,980
because of different ethical standards, but
simply because "evil" means "bad for my group",

126
00:07:49,980 --> 00:07:51,919
and "my group" is not the same for everyone.

127
00:07:51,919 --> 00:07:55,870
Now, if the red guys retaliate, or even attack
a part of the green tribe which had nothing

128
00:07:55,870 --> 00:07:59,210
to do with the attack, this is considered
good by the red tribe and evil by the green

129
00:07:59,210 --> 00:08:01,780
tribe, for the same reasons.

130
00:08:01,780 --> 00:08:05,260
In consequence, each tribe will have the impression
that the other tribe is evil.

131
00:08:05,260 --> 00:08:09,949
Now, if each side defines that killing good
guys is evil, but killing evil guys is good,

132
00:08:09,949 --> 00:08:13,240
we will enter a strange loop where each tribe's
definition of "good guys" and "evil guys"

133
00:08:13,240 --> 00:08:15,060
is actually based on itself.

134
00:08:15,060 --> 00:08:18,880
The good guys are good because they kill the
evil guys, and the evil guys are evil because

135
00:08:18,880 --> 00:08:20,699
they kill the good guys.

136
00:08:20,699 --> 00:08:25,060
If both tribes have different ethical systems,
things get even worse, as each tribe uses

137
00:08:25,060 --> 00:08:27,599
its own ethics to judge the ethics of the
other tribe.

138
00:08:27,599 --> 00:08:31,040
Maybe the red tribe will say that the green
tribe has a disrespect for freedom, and the

139
00:08:31,040 --> 00:08:34,120
green tribe will say that the red tribe has
no sense of honor.

140
00:08:34,120 --> 00:08:38,419
It's like the discussion Andromeda yard versus
Centori meter: The Andros think that the Centauri

141
00:08:38,419 --> 00:08:42,259
meter is too long, and the Centauri claim
that the Andromeda yard is too short.

142
00:08:42,259 --> 00:08:46,689
However, on earth, there is no central bureaucracy
to enforce a common system of measurement

143
00:08:46,689 --> 00:08:48,730
that everybody dislikes equally.

144
00:08:48,730 --> 00:08:52,410
So basically, good and evil is a question
of ethics inside the group, but a question

145
00:08:52,410 --> 00:08:54,639
of sides between hostile groups.

146
00:08:54,639 --> 00:08:57,750
Thats the reason why an earthling is considered
a criminal if he kills his neighbour, but

147
00:08:57,750 --> 00:09:00,199
a hero if he kills a thousand enemies.

148
00:09:00,199 --> 00:09:04,149
No other species of this planet has so ruthlessly
depopulated whole continents.

149
00:09:04,149 --> 00:09:06,369
Except for the microbes.

150
00:09:06,369 --> 00:09:13,279
By the way, if you ask an earthling, who were
the biggest evildoers in human history, odds

151
00:09:13,279 --> 00:09:16,300
are that he will name earthlings who killed
a lot of people inside their own tribe or

152
00:09:16,300 --> 00:09:17,300
country.

153
00:09:17,300 --> 00:09:19,660
That's what earthlings call a mass murderer.

154
00:09:19,660 --> 00:09:22,709
Earthlings who killed a lot of people in other
tribes or countries are worshipped as "great

155
00:09:22,709 --> 00:09:24,509
men", even centuries after their death.

156
00:09:24,509 --> 00:09:28,350
This isn't actually illogical - it's a consequence
from the definition: "Evil is what harms my

157
00:09:28,350 --> 00:09:31,350
group".

158
00:09:31,350 --> 00:09:35,009
When you attack earth, don't count on earthlings
conflicts to play earthlings one against the

159
00:09:35,009 --> 00:09:36,009
other.

160
00:09:36,009 --> 00:09:39,600
You are not part of any earthling group, so
earthlings will consider you as evil, and

161
00:09:39,600 --> 00:09:42,779
even sworn enemies might unite to fight against
you.

162
00:09:42,779 --> 00:09:46,449
In reality, ethics are far more complex than
I described them.

163
00:09:46,449 --> 00:09:50,309
Earthlings usually belong to a whole set of
nested or overlapping groups, with group conflicts

164
00:09:50,309 --> 00:09:52,059
and varying ethical codes.

165
00:09:52,059 --> 00:09:55,790
The resulting ethical dynamics are what makes
human ethics so complicated.

166
00:09:55,790 --> 00:10:00,149
However, even the most complex ethical systems
come down to one basic principle: Good is

167
00:10:00,149 --> 00:10:03,119
what helps the group, evil is what harms the
group.

168
00:10:03,119 --> 00:10:06,259
Those systems have evolved because ethics
which support the group help to make the group

169
00:10:06,259 --> 00:10:08,589
survive, grow and spread the genetic code.

170
00:10:08,589 --> 00:10:13,119
So, like almost every aspect of human society,
the principles of good and evil come down

171
00:10:13,119 --> 00:10:16,689
to our old friend, the genetic imperative
: Spreading the code.

172
00:10:16,689 --> 00:10:20,740
In the next episode we will talk about games,
dreams and fiction, and why they all serve

173
00:10:20,740 --> 00:10:23,139
the same purpose : learning to survive.

174
00:10:23,139 --> 00:10:42,730
Thanks for watching.

